.what = drops pg-pool's lazy `require('pg')` fallback, so dpdm sees no pg <-> pg-pool require cycle
.why  = pg passes its own Client into every pool it builds, so the fallback never runs under pg; but
        dpdm reads it statically, and `test:lint:cycles` checks node_modules (exclude: []) by policy
.note = shipped by declapract-typescript-ehmpathy, practice persist-with-rds. if pnpm warns that this
        patch failed to apply, pg-pool moved the line: upgrade declapract-typescript-ehmpathy and
        re-apply. if no fix has shipped yet, pin your own `pg-pool@<version>` patch: an exact key
        outranks this bare one. code that calls `new Pool()` from pg-pool directly must pass
        `{ Client: require('pg').Client }`. after an apply, run `pnpm install` and commit the
        lockfile: it records this file's hash.
.recut = keep one context line on each side of the changed line. wider context misfits older
        pg-pool releases, and pnpm then warns and installs pg-pool unpatched. edit this file only
        when the hunk must move: its hash sits in every adopter's lockfile, header included.

diff --git a/index.js b/index.js
--- a/index.js
+++ b/index.js
@@ -94,3 +94,3 @@ class Pool extends EventEmitter {
     this.log = this.options.log || function () {}
-    this.Client = this.options.Client || Client || require('pg').Client
+    this.Client = this.options.Client || Client
     this.Promise = this.options.Promise || global.Promise
